   "answer": "RAPTOR first embeds each 100‑token text chunk with SBERT (multi‑qa‑mpnet‑base‑cos‑v1) and then groups the resulting vectors using a clustering algorithm that organizes chunks into cohesive clusters based on semantic similarity【1】.  \nThe clustering step employs a soft‑clustering approach, allowing a node to belong to multiple clusters and not requiring a fixed number of clusters【2】.  \nClusters are formed recursively: chunks that are clustered together become sibling leaf nodes, and a parent node is created that contains a language‑model‑generated summary of that cluster, enabling the tree to be built bottom‑up【3】【8】.",
